              <zone forceUpdate='true' h='49779' id='13' type-v2='text' w='18900' x='80632' y='17589'>
                <formatted-text>
                  <run>📶 Map Explanation&#10;&#10;</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000'>This map uses 2024 Census Data to estimate individuals at or below 125% of the Federal Poverty Limit compared to estimated individuals enrolled on SNAP to highlight gaps in participation by zip code.</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000'>Highest opportunity category shows areas with less then 50% snap participation and 20% or greater of population at or below 125% FPL.</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000'>Remaining categories highlight different ranges of SNAP participation where % at or below 125% FPL is at least 10%.</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000'>Please use filters below to filter both map and table together.</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000'>❕Note:</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000'>Estimates of individuals on SNAP are based on household enrollments (X) avg. HH size. </run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000'>This does not represent actual SNAP enrollment numbers and only provides a relative estimation of SNAP participation compared to other zip codes in the area. Few areas may show outlier participation rates that reflect margin of error with this method.</run>
                </formatted-text>
                <zone-style>
                  <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                  <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                  <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                  <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                </zone-style>
              </zone>
            </zone>
          </zone>
